Multishine card loader, stage 1 (NTSC 1.02 only), loader flavour: the save carries ONLY the exploit, the UCF 0.84 copy table and codehandler,
and a ~2 KB card code loader (offline/cardloader/cl/).  The codeset itself, the Slippi payloads and later the whole engine are NOT in this
file: the loader reads them from the card file MultishineCode (docs/design/CARD_PACKAGE.md), so a code change is a small card-file upload
and never touches this save.  Generated by offline/cardloader/build_cardpkg.py from this template (@CLBIN@ = the linked loader image).

!begin

!src "../../third_party/melee-gci-compiler/ucf0.84/ucf_data/ace_exploit.mgc"
!src "../../third_party/melee-gci-compiler/ucf0.84/ucf_data/datacopy_table.mgc"

@COPYFIX@
!loc 8046180c
# internal save name Melee uses after the loader ran (0x18 bytes, NUL padded; offline/projname.py SHORT + "Melee")
@SAVENAME@

!loc 80461824
# displayed save name (0x0c bytes; SHORT)
@DISPNAME@

!loc 80461830
00 34 01 02 04 00 0a 00 08 01 01 00

!loc 80460c64
!bin "@HANDLER@"

# v1.02 Gecko list: UCF's framing (one-shot block, card-unplug guard, no game-data re-init, Tournament Melee loads VS), then ONE C0 code = the loader
!loc 80465000
00d0c0de 00d0c0de
22000034 @LIST@
0401c638 38000004
0401c63c 901f0008
041a4234 60000000
04000034 @LIST@
0422d638 38000002
c0000000 @CLLINES@
!bin "@CLBIN@"
e2000001 00000000
f0000000 00000000

# v1.01 / v1.00 codesets: UCF's, unchanged (we only target 1.02)
!loc 8045e6e0
!src "../../third_party/melee-gci-compiler/ucf0.84/ucf_data/ntsc1.01/codeset_v101.mgc"
!loc 80468c64
!src "../../third_party/melee-gci-compiler/ucf0.84/ucf_data/ntsc1.00/codeset_v100.mgc"
